{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p27-caab5838","text":"The audit is essentially complete. Everything is implemented. The genuine gaps I've identified:

1. **PatientRegistry table column misalignment** — "Actions" th before "Gender" th in the header, but body renders Gender before Actions. Real bug, will fix.

2. **Missing admin user provisioning UI (POST /api/users)** — the users page has list/approve only. The master prompt says "Implement all supported create, read, update, delete, activation, approval, rejection... operations that are actually available in the current API and UI design." POST /api/users is available (ADMIN, `users:manage`). The master plan flags it as a product decision, but the completion directive takes precedence: complete all supported operations. I'll add a "Create user" form to the users page wired to POST /api/users, following the same in-page Card form pattern used by PatientRegistry/DoctorDirectory.

3. **PatientRegistry medicalHistory in create payload** — need to verify patient.validation.ts accepts `medicalHistory` on create. Let me check the patient validation schema to confirm the create payload fields (patientCode, name, email, phone, dateOfBirth, gender, medicalHistory).

Also, let me double check `src/app/doctors/[id]/DoctorDetail.tsx` and the remaining pages (patients/page.tsx, doctors/page.tsx, schedules/page.tsx, departments/page.tsx, ot-rooms/page.tsx, equipment/page.tsx, patients/appointments pages) — they're likely thin wrappers with guards. The master plan already verified them. Let me spot-check a couple quickly and check the patient validation schema.

4. The **UserList "Rejected/activation"** operations: the master prompt mentions activation/rejection for user management. The API only supports approve for pending patients (`/api/users/{id}/approve`); there's no user status PATCH endpoint (only doctors have status endpoint). So no user suspend/reject UI — correctly absent since the API doesn't support it. Document as backend-dependent gap.

