## 2. Patient workflow — verified in an isolated incognito tab

Signed in as seeded patient `sarah.patient@example.test`:
- `/login` → `/dashboard` with PATIENT role, nav scoped to Dashboard + My Appointments only
- Dashboard shows **only their own** appointment; the foreign schedule for another patient is absent
- Foreign/staff APIs return **403**: `/api/users`, `/api/schedules`, `/api/departments`, `/api/ot-rooms`, `/api/equipment`, `/api/audit-logs`
- Empty state renders when no upcoming appointments
- Both desktop and mobile viewports checked; sidebar docked correctly with no overflow

**Known issue (documented, not introduced by Phase 3):** after sign-out, the tab lands on a Chromium error page because `NEXTAUTH_URL` is set to port 3000 while the server runs on 3210. This was already in the Phase 2 tracker and is unchanged.

## 3. Database test status — resolved, isolated DB used

The failing database test (`alerts-repository-audit`) was failing because it defaulted to the **shared** `medorch-postgres` container and crashed on duplicate fixture emails. Now it requires an explicit isolated `DATABASE_URL` and skips cleanly without one. Verified on **fresh disposable containers** (created, migrated, tested, removed — `medorch-postgres` was never touched):

